  "gaps": [
    "The capture contains several programs (end of Cybersecurity Technology, full BS in Data Science, and BA in East Asian Studies); the request did not name one, so this ledger assumes the BS in Data Science. Confirm the intended program.",
    "The elective credit amount of 40 is not printed. It is derived as 75 (printed 'Remaining General Education and Elective Courses') minus the 35 general-education credits not already covered by the related courses. It assumes MATH 115 fills the 3-credit Mathematics requirement and DATA 200 fills the 3-credit computing portion of Research and Computing Literacy, as the course-sequencing table indicates.",
    "The General Education Mathematics (3) and computing/IT (3) blocks are not listed separately, to avoid double counting with the related courses MATH 115 and DATA 200.",
    "Residency rules are program-wide credit counts, not course-specific: at least 30 credits (normally the final 30) at UMGC, half of major credits at UMGC, and at least 15 upper-level credits at UMGC. No individual course is marked as required at UMGC, so institutionalOnly is false throughout.",
    "Grade rules: minimum grade of C for major courses, 2.0 overall GPA, and WRTG 112 with C- or better within the first 24 credits. Mathematics must be completed within the first 24 credits. Pass/fail electives are capped at 18 credits.",
    "Catalog year is printed as spaced characters ('2 0 2 6 – 2 0 2 7'). The requirements apply to students beginning continuous enrollment on or after August 1, 2026."
  ],
